  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under IRC Section 469(g)(1), a fully taxable disposition of an entire passive activity interest releases all suspended passive losses. By electing out of installment treatment under Section 453(d), Gallagher recognizes the full $160,000 gain and triggers immediate release of all $145,000 in suspended losses, netting only $15,000 of taxable gain in the current year.
Wrong (A): While installment reporting spreads gain, it proportionally defers the loss release benefit, eliminating the immediate offset advantage.
Wrong (B): Suspended losses are not released proportionally under the installment method; they are fully released upon a complete disposition regardless of payment timing.
Wrong (C): Released suspended losses remain passive in character and do not convert to portfolio deductions.$EXPL$
