  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under Treas. Reg. Section 1.469-2(f)(6), rental income from property rented to a business in which the taxpayer materially participates is recharacterized as nonpassive income. This self-rental rule prevents taxpayers from generating artificial passive income to shelter passive losses from other activities.
Wrong (A): The self-rental rule specifically recharacterizes this income as nonpassive, so it cannot absorb passive losses from other activities.
Wrong (B): Rental income from real property is not portfolio income. Portfolio income includes interest, dividends, and royalties reported on Schedule B.
Wrong (D): The rental income is fully taxable; there is no provision classifying self-rental income as tax-exempt.$EXPL$
