  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under IRC Section 469(k), passive losses from a publicly traded partnership can only offset passive income from that same PTP. Because PTP Beta generated no income of its own in 2026, the entire $18,000 loss is suspended and carried forward to future years.
Wrong (A): PTP losses cannot cross over to offset income from a different PTP. Each PTP is treated as a separate basket under Section 469(k).
Wrong (C): This incorrectly combines PTP netting across entities. PTP Beta losses cannot offset PTP Alpha income or private partnership income.
