  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under IRC Section 401(a) and ERISA Title IV, the Pension Benefit Guaranty Corporation insures defined benefit plans, guaranteeing participants receive promised benefits up to a statutory maximum if the plan terminates with insufficient assets. This protection exists because defined benefit plans promise a specific benefit amount.
Wrong (B): Defined contribution plans like 401(k)s are not insured by the PBGC because participants bear investment risk and there is no promised benefit amount to guarantee.
Wrong (C): IRAs are individual accounts, not employer-sponsored defined benefit plans, and are not covered by PBGC insurance.
