-- Q7776: Retirement Plans and Education Savings [medium/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under IRC Section 72(t)(2)(A)(iv) and IRS Notice 2022-6, the fixed amortization method generally produces the largest SEPP payments because it amortizes the account balance over life expectancy using a reasonable interest rate, yielding a higher fixed annual amount than the other approved methods.
Wrong (A): The required minimum distribution method produces the smallest payments because it divides only by the life expectancy factor without incorporating an interest rate component.
Wrong (B): There is no IRS-approved SEPP method called the "modified endowment contract method." The three methods are RMD, fixed amortization, and fixed annuitization.
